Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (AC49, AC50, AC51, AC52)
Research: Q8 (AC50 on the recorded tool_turn fixture); Q3 (real Claude Code resends stay AC61's manual check); Q13 (the known core flake hit one make verify run)
Why this approach: the tests live in pipeline_test.go next to TestParse_FailureKeepsRaw and reuse its capturing gateway; a post helper takes the nth access-log line's request_id, since requests go one at a time. "One stored copy" is checked as one content row for the hash (a read-only SQL count; the store package's sqlite driver is already linked) plus Reader.Content resolving it. AC50 and AC51 share runToolTurn: turn 1 is next_request.json cut before the assistant message and re-encoded compact, answered with the recorded response.sse; turn 2 is next_request.json as recorded, so system and tools differ in bytes (compact vs pretty) but not in content. AC49 resends a message with a block over 4096 bytes (blob path), as sent and in a cache_control_added subtest (pretty-printed, keys reordered, cache_control on the block). AC52 checks a nested and an input-top-level cache_control.
Alternatives rejected: a separate dedup_test.go (the task names pipeline_test.go); exposing a content-count method on store.Reader (production API for a test only).
Trade-off / known limit: the one-row count is guaranteed by the content table's primary key, so the load-bearing assertions are the equal hashes; no T4 or T20 bug was found.
Verified by: all four passed on arrival; proved by temporarily breaking internal/core/canonical.go three ways, then restoring it: excluding cache_control at any depth of verbatim content failed TestStore_ExclusionNotAppliedInsideToolInput (both subtests); dropping the object and entries exclusions failed TestStore_BlockContentDedup/cache_control_added; a per-call hash suffix failed TestStore_BlockContentDedup, TestStore_ResponseMessageDedupsWithNextRequest and TestStore_SystemAndToolsStoredOnce. make verify passed (one earlier run hit Q13's TestAccessLog_UpstreamAbortedField/completed flake in internal/core, untouched here; 5 reruns and the next make verify passed).
